Ancient and medieval histories (@ancient-and-medieval-histories: 0, is #chapter, #outline) { r_2VMGX2WRN4DJECEMHJMTZTAESX
This material investigates ancient and medieval societies through their sources, material conditions, institutions, beliefs, conflicts, and exchanges. Connect settlements, states, labour, trade, technologies, intellectual life, and changing political or religious arrangements across selected regions and periods. Build routes around a society, relationship, or transformation rather than assuming one universal sequence of development. Introduce source interpretation and chronology as needed, and connect the historical setting of philosophical and literary works to the wider society that sustained them.

**Parent:** [History](../History.lingua#r_3MKG6XS2X0W9YR8T4438CTGZ1T).
